1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Monday, 8 a.m. The ticket gates.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,567
Whoa! That's a 30x fine! Where's your conscience?!

3
00:00:05,567 --> 00:00:08,300
Moragu, duck. You're still a baby.

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,633
Dad, I'm eight.

5
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:14,800
Passenger, an announcement: it's only free until age six.

6
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:15,467
…Yes, ma'am.

7
00:00:15,467 --> 00:00:20,033
Others sneak through: a crime. My son: still a baby. Double standard, number one.

8
00:00:20,033 --> 00:00:22,167
I'm… Modapman.

9
00:00:22,167 --> 00:00:25,867
If I do it, so what. If you do it: rude! The public transit edition.

10
00:00:25,867 --> 00:00:30,433
This stop is… Double Standard Station. Doors open on the conscience side.

11
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:32,067
Round one: seats.

12
00:00:32,067 --> 00:00:36,533
Look at her. Saving a seat with her bag. That's privatizing a seat!

13
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:41,700
An empty seat! Mo takes a 3-meter run-up! Half twist in the air… and he's seated!

14
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:44,000
This one's my son's. So what~

15
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,033
Dad, I can stand. Let that grandpa sit.

16
00:00:48,033 --> 00:00:53,733
Their bag: seat privatization. My bag: a family reservation. Double standard, number two.

17
00:00:53,733 --> 00:00:59,433
Passenger. Just one bag and people avoid that seat. It's called territorial marking.

18
00:00:59,433 --> 00:01:01,333
…You're on the train too?

19
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:02,867
Round two: fake sleeping.

20
00:01:02,867 --> 00:01:07,900
Look, the moment grandma got on, he shut his eyes. Award-winning acting.

21
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,033
Oh, my legs…

22
00:01:09,033 --> 00:01:13,667
I am in a deep sleep… zzz…

23
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:15,133
When grandma gets off at the next stop—

24
00:01:15,133 --> 00:01:17,967
Oh? What a nap~ So what~

25
00:01:17,967 --> 00:01:22,600
They sleep: best actor. I sleep: a real blackout. Double standard, number three.

26
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:29,467
Passenger. Seniors, pregnant women, people with small kids: the law calls them mobility-impaired. That's the seat you give up.

27
00:01:29,467 --> 00:01:30,933
Round three: phone calls.

28
00:01:30,933 --> 00:01:35,233
Listen to him on the phone. The whole car can hear. Noise pollution.

29
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:38,200
Yes! Sir! Yes, yes! That Excel file! Yes!

30
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:41,600
The entire car… is now waiting for that Excel file.

31
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,467
Work calls can't be helped. So what~

32
00:01:44,467 --> 00:01:48,600
Their call: noise pollution. My call: business. Double standard, number four.

33
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:55,400
Passenger. Hearing one side of a call is more distracting than a whole conversation. It's called a halfalogue.

34
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:58,833
You can't guess what comes next, so your ears keep listening!

35
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:02,100
Round four: the transfer bus, and coffee.

36
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:08,367
Yesterday someone spilled a latte on the bus and soaked my pants. Boarding with a cup is terrorism.

37
00:02:08,367 --> 00:02:11,400
But this is a work essential. So what~

38
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,733
Passenger, that cup can't ride.

39
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:15,267
…You're here TOO?!

40
00:02:15,267 --> 00:02:16,367
I'm her younger sister.

41
00:02:16,433 --> 00:02:20,933
Their cup: terrorism. My cup: an essential. Double standard, number five.

42
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:28,367
Seoul city buses can refuse disposable cups with drinks in them. A sealed tumbler is fine.

43
00:02:28,367 --> 00:02:31,833
…Brain freeze.

44
00:02:31,833 --> 00:02:34,033
Bonus round. Rapid-fire double standards!

45
00:02:34,033 --> 00:02:37,100
Their backpack: a weapon. Mine: hiking vibes!

46
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:40,800
They're loud: a fish market. My old classmates: reliving memories!

47
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:44,200
They play videos out loud: rude. Me: my earbuds died!

48
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:47,133
Double standard: six, seven, eight!

49
00:02:47,133 --> 00:02:50,600
Dad, that grandma said her legs hurt.

50
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,667
…Yeah.

51
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:56,900
The subway is a living room we all share. You'll want a seat too when you're a grandpa.

52
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,233
…Okay. Starting tomorrow, I'll stand.

53
00:02:59,233 --> 00:03:01,433
That evening, the bus home.

54
00:03:01,433 --> 00:03:04,733
An exhausted Mo, out cold three seconds after sitting down.

55
00:03:04,733 --> 00:03:13,633
Manspreading, one. Backpack, two. Coffee, three. Video sound, four. Snoring, five.

56
00:03:13,633 --> 00:03:18,300
Passenger, an announcement: today's all-in-one nuisance combo.

57
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:21,233
Honey! Where are you?! Dinner's cold!

58
00:03:21,233 --> 00:03:24,267
…I'm just tired. So what.

59
00:03:24,267 --> 00:03:28,933
Others do it: a nuisance. I do it: I'm tired. Double standard, nine and ten.

60
00:03:28,933 --> 00:03:32,800
This stop is the last stop: Conscience Station. Just a wrong answer.

61
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:35,367
…Classic Modapman.
